# Audio2Face-3D Blender Addon — Product Requirements Document & Roadmap
# Version: 1.0 | Date: 2026-02-24

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## PART 1: PRODUCT DEFINITION

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

### 1.1 Product Name
Audio2Face for Blender (working title)
- Internal codename: "a2f-blender"
- Blender extension ID: "nvidia_audio2face"
- bl_idname prefix: "A2F"

### 1.2 One-Line Description
AI-powered facial animation from audio — full 52-blendshape face performance
including lip-sync, emotion, brows, cheeks, and jaw — directly inside Blender.

### 1.3 Target Users
- Primary: Blender animators who need lip-sync / facial animation for characters
- Primary: Game developers using Blender in their pipeline (batch NPC dialogue)
- Primary: VTuber / virtual content creators ($3-7B market, 45% indie, most use Blender)
- Secondary: Indie filmmakers, virtual production artists, arch-viz
- Funnel: Hobbyists and learners (free tier → paid conversion)

### 1.4 User Personas

#### Persona A: "Solo Animator"
- Uses Blender for character animation, short films
- Has a character with ARKit blendshapes (from Mixamo, ReadyPlayerMe, or custom)
- Currently hand-animates lip-sync or uses Rhubarb (tedious)
- Wants: one-click audio → facial animation
- Tech comfort: moderate (can install addons, not comfortable with Docker/CLI)

#### Persona B: "Indie Game Dev"
- Exports from Blender to Unity/Unreal
- Characters use ARKit blendshapes (MetaHuman-compatible)
- Needs batch processing of dialogue lines
- Wants: fast iteration, consistent quality across many lines
- Tech comfort: high (comfortable with APIs, may run local NIM)

#### Persona C: "VTuber / Content Creator"
- Has a VRM/VRChat avatar with custom blendshapes
- Needs pre-recorded facial animation for videos
- Non-standard blendshape names (Japanese, custom naming)
- Wants: works with their specific model, easy mapping
- Tech comfort: low-moderate

