## PART 4: PROPERTIES SPECIFICATION

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

### 4.1 Scene Property Group: A2F_PG_properties

```python
class A2F_PG_properties(bpy.types.PropertyGroup):

    # ── Core Settings ──
    audio_file: StringProperty(
        name="Audio File",
        description="Path to WAV audio file (PCM 16-bit, mono or stereo)",
        subtype='FILE_PATH',
        default="",
    )
    target_mesh: PointerProperty(
        name="Target Mesh",
        description="Mesh object to apply facial animation to",
        type=bpy.types.Object,
        poll=lambda self, obj: obj.type == 'MESH',
    )
    model: EnumProperty(
        name="Model",
        description="Audio2Face-3D model to use for generation",
        items=[
            ('james_v2.3', "James v2.3", "English male, strong emotion expression"),
            ('claire_v2.3', "Claire v2.3", "Chinese + English female voice"),
            ('mark_v2.3', "Mark v2.3", "English male, high-resolution geometry"),
        ],
        default='james_v2.3',
    )
    frame_start: IntProperty(
        name="Frame Start",
        description="Frame number where animation begins on the timeline",
        default=1,
        min=0,
    )

    # ── Generation State ──
    is_generating: BoolProperty(default=False, options={'HIDDEN', 'SKIP_SAVE'})
    generation_progress: FloatProperty(default=0.0, min=0.0, max=1.0, options={'HIDDEN', 'SKIP_SAVE'})
    last_status: StringProperty(default="Ready", options={'SKIP_SAVE'})
    last_frame_count: IntProperty(default=0, options={'SKIP_SAVE'})

    # ── Connection ──
    connection_mode: EnumProperty(
        name="Connection Mode",
        items=[
            ('CLOUD', "Cloud API", "Use NVIDIA's hosted cloud API (grpc.nvcf.nvidia.com)"),
            ('LOCAL', "Local Server", "Connect to a local or self-hosted NIM server"),
        ],
        default='CLOUD',
    )
    server_url: StringProperty(
        name="Server URL",
        description="Address of local Audio2Face-3D NIM server",
        default="localhost:52000",
    )

    # ── Emotion Controls ──
    auto_emotion: BoolProperty(
        name="Auto-Detect Emotion",
        description="Let Audio2Emotion detect emotion from the audio automatically",
        default=True,
    )
    emotion_strength: FloatProperty(name="Emotion Strength", default=0.6, min=0.0, max=2.0, step=10)
    emotion_contrast: FloatProperty(name="Emotion Contrast", default=1.0, min=0.0, max=3.0, step=10)
    max_emotions: IntProperty(name="Max Emotions", default=3, min=1, max=10)

    # Manual emotion overrides (0.0 = not set, passthrough to auto)
    emotion_joy: FloatProperty(name="Joy", default=0.0, min=0.0, max=1.0, step=10)
    emotion_anger: FloatProperty(name="Anger", default=0.0, min=0.0, max=1.0, step=10)
    emotion_sadness: FloatProperty(name="Sadness", default=0.0, min=0.0, max=1.0, step=10)
    emotion_fear: FloatProperty(name="Fear", default=0.0, min=0.0, max=1.0, step=10)
    emotion_amazement: FloatProperty(name="Amazement", default=0.0, min=0.0, max=1.0, step=10)
    emotion_disgust: FloatProperty(name="Disgust", default=0.0, min=0.0, max=1.0, step=10)
    emotion_cheekiness: FloatProperty(name="Cheekiness", default=0.0, min=0.0, max=1.0, step=10)
    emotion_grief: FloatProperty(name="Grief", default=0.0, min=0.0, max=1.0, step=10)
    emotion_pain: FloatProperty(name="Pain", default=0.0, min=0.0, max=1.0, step=10)
    emotion_outofbreath: FloatProperty(name="Out of Breath", default=0.0, min=0.0, max=1.0, step=10)

    # ── Face Parameters ──
    skin_strength: FloatProperty(name="Skin Strength", default=1.0, min=0.0, max=3.0, step=10)
    upper_face_strength: FloatProperty(name="Upper Face Strength", default=1.0, min=0.0, max=3.0, step=10)
    upper_face_smoothing: FloatProperty(name="Upper Face Smoothing", default=0.001, min=0.0, max=0.1, step=1, precision=4)
    lower_face_strength: FloatProperty(name="Lower Face Strength", default=1.2, min=0.0, max=3.0, step=10)
    lower_face_smoothing: FloatProperty(name="Lower Face Smoothing", default=0.006, min=0.0, max=0.1, step=1, precision=4)
    face_mask_level: FloatProperty(name="Face Mask Level", default=0.6, min=0.0, max=1.0, step=10)
    face_mask_softness: FloatProperty(name="Face Mask Softness", default=0.0085, min=0.0, max=0.1, step=1, precision=4)
    eyelid_open_offset: FloatProperty(name="Eyelid Open Offset", default=0.06, min=-0.5, max=0.5, step=1)
    lip_open_offset: FloatProperty(name="Lip Open Offset", default=-0.02, min=-0.5, max=0.5, step=1)

    # ── Mapping ──
    mapping_preset: EnumProperty(
        name="Mapping Preset",
        items=[
            ('ARKIT', "ARKit (Standard)", "Standard ARKit blendshape names (MetaHuman, RPM compatible)"),
            ('VRM', "VRM / VRChat", "VRM blendshape naming convention"),
            ('CUSTOM', "Custom", "Use custom name mapping"),
        ],
        default='ARKIT',
    )
    mapping_items: CollectionProperty(type=A2F_PG_mapping_item)
    mapping_items_index: IntProperty(default=0)
```

### 4.2 Mapping Item Property Group: A2F_PG_mapping_item

```python
class A2F_PG_mapping_item(bpy.types.PropertyGroup):
    arkit_name: StringProperty(name="ARKit Name")
    blender_name: StringProperty(name="Blender Shape Key", default="")
    enabled: BoolProperty(name="Enabled", default=True)
    multiplier: FloatProperty(name="Multiplier", default=1.0, min=0.0, max=5.0)
```

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## PART 5: ERROR HANDLING SPECIFICATION

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

### 5.1 User-Facing Errors (self.report)

| Condition | Level | Message |
|-----------|-------|---------|
| No audio file selected | ERROR | "No audio file selected. Please choose a WAV file." |
| Audio file not found | ERROR | "Audio file not found: {path}" |
| Audio not WAV format | ERROR | "Unsupported audio format. Please use WAV (PCM 16-bit)." |
| Audio not 16-bit PCM | ERROR | "Audio must be 16-bit PCM WAV. Current: {bit_depth}-bit" |
| Audio > 5 minutes | ERROR | "Audio exceeds 5 minute limit ({duration:.1f}s). Please use a shorter clip." |
| Audio > 2 channels | ERROR | "Only mono or stereo audio supported. File has {channels} channels." |
| No target mesh | ERROR | "No target mesh selected. Please select a mesh object." |
| Mesh has no shape keys | WARNING | "Target mesh has no shape keys. Click 'Create Shape Keys' first." |
| No API key (cloud mode) | ERROR | "No API key configured. Get one free at build.nvidia.com" |
| Connection failed | ERROR | "Cannot connect to Audio2Face service: {details}" |
| Connection timeout | ERROR | "Connection timed out after 10 seconds. Check your network/server." |
| gRPC error | ERROR | "Audio2Face service error: {grpc_details}" |
| Generation already running | WARNING | "Generation already in progress. Please wait." |
| No animation data | WARNING | "No animation data to preview. Generate animation first." |
| Server returned error | ERROR | "Server error: {status_message}" |
| Stereo auto-converted | INFO | "Stereo audio auto-converted to mono." |
| Resampled | INFO | "Audio resampled from {original}Hz to 16000Hz." |
| Shape keys created | INFO | "Created {N} ARKit shape keys on {mesh_name}." |
| Generation success | INFO | "Generated {N} frames of facial animation ({duration:.1f}s)." |
| Mapping complete | INFO | "Mapped {N}/52 shape keys. {M} unmapped." |
| Animation cleared | INFO | "Cleared animation from {N} shape keys." |
| Connection OK | INFO | "Successfully connected to Audio2Face service." |

### 5.2 Internal Error Handling

- All gRPC calls wrapped in try/except grpc.aio.AioRpcError
- Background thread exceptions caught and stored in GenerationState.error_message
- Timer callback checks for errors and reports to user
- Never let an exception propagate uncaught in background thread (would be silent)
- Log all errors to Blender console if log_level >= INFO

### 5.3 Network Retry Logic
- Health check: single attempt, 5s timeout
- Generation stream: single attempt, no retry (user can click Generate again)
- If gRPC UNAVAILABLE: suggest checking network/server
- If gRPC UNAUTHENTICATED: suggest checking API key
- If gRPC RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED: suggest "API credits may be exhausted"

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## PART 6: DEPENDENCY MANAGEMENT

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

### 6.1 Required Dependencies

| Package | Version | Size | Why | Bundled How |
|---------|---------|------|-----|-------------|
| grpcio | >=1.64.1 | ~3MB | gRPC runtime | Wheel in wheels/ |
| protobuf | >=5.27 | ~400KB | Protobuf runtime | Wheel in wheels/ |
| numpy | any | — | Audio processing | Already in Blender |
| nvidia_ace stubs | — | ~200KB | Protobuf stubs | Copied into vendor/ |

### 6.2 NOT Required (Avoiding Bloat)

| Package | Why Not | Alternative |
|---------|---------|-------------|
| scipy | 30MB, only needed for resampling | numpy linear interpolation |
| soundfile | Needs libsndfile binary | Python stdlib `wave` module |
| pyyaml | Only NVIDIA samples use it for config | We use Python dicts directly |
| pandas | Only NVIDIA samples use for CSV export | Python stdlib `csv` module |

### 6.3 Wheel Strategy for Blender Extension

blender_manifest.toml:
```toml
[permissions]
network = "Connect to NVIDIA Audio2Face-3D service for AI facial animation"
files = "Read audio files and export animation data"

wheels = [
    "./wheels/grpcio-1.64.1-cp311-cp311-manylinux_2_17_x86_64.whl",
    "./wheels/grpcio-1.64.1-cp311-cp311-win_amd64.whl",
    "./wheels/grpcio-1.64.1-cp311-cp311-macosx_10_9_universal2.whl",
    "./wheels/protobuf-5.27.0-cp311-cp311-manylinux2014_x86_64.whl",
    "./wheels/protobuf-5.27.0-cp311-cp311-win_amd64.whl",
    "./wheels/protobuf-5.27.0-cp311-cp311-macosx_10_9_universal2.whl",
]
```

Note: Must bundle wheels for all platforms (linux-x64, win-amd64, macos-arm64/x64).
Blender 4.2+ uses Python 3.11. Check exact version per Blender release.

### 6.4 Vendor Directory (nvidia_ace stubs)
Copy from Maya-ACE `python/grpc_py/nvidia_ace/` (MIT licensed):
- Rename import paths to be relative within our addon
- Or add vendor/ to sys.path at register time:
  ```python
  import sys, os
  vendor_path = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), "vendor")
  if vendor_path not in sys.path:
      sys.path.insert(0, vendor_path)
  ```

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

## PART 7: IMPLEMENTATION ROADMAP

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

### Milestone 1: "Hello gRPC" — Prove the Connection Works
Priority: CRITICAL | Ship-blocking

Tasks:
  1.1  Create addon package skeleton
       - __init__.py with bl_info and blender_manifest.toml
       - register() / unregister() with reload support
       - Empty operators.py, panels.py, properties.py, preferences.py, constants.py

  1.2  Implement constants.py
       - ARKIT_BLENDSHAPE_NAMES: tuple of 52 strings in NVIDIA's exact order
       - EMOTION_NAMES: tuple of 10 strings
       - DEFAULT_MULTIPLIERS: dict per model (james, claire, mark)
       - DEFAULT_OFFSETS: dict (all 0.0)
       - DEFAULT_FACE_PARAMS: dict with 9 face parameter defaults
       - DEFAULT_POST_PROCESSING: dict with 6 emotion post-processing defaults

  1.3  Copy nvidia_ace protobuf stubs into vendor/
       - From Maya-ACE python/grpc_py/nvidia_ace/
       - Fix import paths (add vendor/ to sys.path in __init__.py)
       - Verify stubs load without error

  1.4  Implement core/client.py — minimal gRPC client
       - Function: create_channel(mode, api_key, function_id, server_url) → channel
       - Function: health_check(channel) → bool
       - Function: generate(channel, audio_bytes, sample_rate, config) → list of frames
       - All async, designed to run in asyncio.run() from a thread

  1.5  Implement preferences.py
       - A2F_AP_preferences with api_key, function_id, connection_mode, server_url

  1.6  Implement basic properties.py
       - A2F_PG_properties with audio_file, target_mesh, connection_mode, server_url

  1.7  Implement A2F_OT_test_connection operator
       - Runs health check in background thread
       - Reports result to user

  1.8  Implement minimal panel with just Test Connection button
       - Verify end-to-end: addon loads → user enters API key → clicks test → gets "Connected"

  Milestone 1 Exit Criteria:
  ✓ Addon installs in Blender 4.2+ without errors
  ✓ API key can be entered in preferences
  ✓ Test Connection successfully reaches grpc.nvcf.nvidia.com:443
  ✓ Health check returns "SERVING"

---

### Milestone 2: "Audio In, Weights Out" — Core Generation Pipeline
Priority: CRITICAL | Ship-blocking

Tasks:
  2.1  Implement core/audio.py
       - load_wav(filepath) → (sample_rate, data_int16, num_channels)
       - convert_to_mono(data, num_channels) → mono_data
       - resample(data, original_rate, target_rate=16000) → resampled_data
       - chunk_audio(data, sample_rate) → list of bytes chunks
       - validate_audio(filepath) → (ok, error_message)

  2.2  Implement full core/client.py generate function
       - Build AudioStreamHeader from addon properties + constants
       - Stream audio chunks with emotion data on first chunk
       - Receive animation data stream header (extract blendshape names)
       - Receive animation data frames (extract timecodes + weights)
       - Handle status response
       - Return structured GenerationState

  2.3  Implement A2F_OT_generate operator
       - Validate all inputs
       - Load and process audio
       - Start background thread with gRPC call
       - Register timer to poll results
       - Apply animation on completion

  2.4  Implement core/animation.py
       - apply_animation(mesh, frames, mapping, scene_fps, frame_offset)
       - Convert A2F 30 FPS timecodes to Blender frame numbers
       - Insert keyframes per shape key per frame
       - Set interpolation to LINEAR

  2.5  Add progress reporting
       - Window manager progress bar during generation
       - Status text in panel updates during generation

  Milestone 2 Exit Criteria:
  ✓ Select audio WAV + mesh → click Generate → keyframes appear on timeline
  ✓ Shape keys animate when scrubbing timeline
  ✓ Works with both cloud API and local server
  ✓ Progress bar shows during generation
  ✓ Errors are reported clearly to user

