### Milestone 6: "Offline & Scale" — Local SDK + Batch (v1.1)
Priority: HIGH | De-risks NVIDIA dependency + unlocks studio revenue

Tasks:
  6.1  Local C++ SDK backend
       - ctypes wrapper for libaudio2x.so / audio2x.dll
       - Model download from HuggingFace (open-sourced ONNX-TRT, ~2-5 GB)
       - TensorRT engine building
       - Requires: RTX 30xx/40xx, ~3-4 GB VRAM
       - **This is the paid tier's key selling point** — no internet, no API key, faster
       - NOTE: Elevated from "stretch goal" because NVIDIA open-sourced everything in late 2025

  6.2  Batch processing mode
       - Select folder of WAV files → generate all, export CSV per file
       - **This is the feature that converts indie users into studio purchasers**
       - Enables "Studio" pricing tier ($79-99)

  6.3  NLA strip support
       - Push generated animation to NLA strip for layering

  6.4  Audio playback sync in viewport
       - Play audio while previewing animation

### Milestone 7: "Expand" — Post-Launch (v1.2+)
Priority: MEDIUM | Future

Tasks:
  7.1  v3.0 model support
       - Multiple character identities
       - Geometry output (direct vertex positions, not just blendshapes)

  7.2  Blender Extensions platform listing (free tier)
       - Submit to extensions.blender.org once stable
       - Must be GPL — this is the top-of-funnel distribution play

  7.3  MP3/OGG/FLAC audio support
       - WAV-only will be the #1 user complaint
       - Add conversion via ffmpeg subprocess or bundled decoder
       - If can't bundle: provide clear error message with conversion instructions

  7.4  Additional mapping presets
       - Ship presets for popular character models: VRoid, MakeHuman, MB-Lab
       - Reduces shape key mapping support burden

